{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">RGB-VALUE function</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310534","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/RGB-VALUE-function.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/RGB-VALUE-function.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">RGB-VALUE function</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__section_N10024_N10021_N10001\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Returns an INTEGER value that represents a\ncombination of a red, green, and blue color value. This function\nallows you to define an arbitrary color, expanding beyond those\ncolors defined in the color table. </p>\n      <div class=\"note note note_note\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__note_N1002E_N10024_N10021_N10001\"><span class=\"note__title\">Note:</span> Does\nnot apply to SpeedScript programming.</div>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__syntax_GC1A1662702800\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d492018e99\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__idGDO2WN2676086\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>RGB-VALUE ( <var class=\"keyword varname\">redval</var> , <var class=\"keyword varname\">greenval</var> , <var class=\"keyword varname\">blueval</var> )</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">redval</var>, <var class=\"keyword varname\">greenval</var>, <var class=\"keyword varname\">blueval</var></dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">Identifies red, green, and blue color values which can be combined to\ndefine a unique color value.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__example_GC1A1672702810\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d492018e154\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">The\nfollowing code fragment shows how to set the background color of\nan ActiveX control: </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__idGDO2WO2676094\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE hdlControl AS COM-HANDLE NO-UNDO.\n\n/* Complete code to get a handle to a control in a control-frame.*/\n. . .\nhdlControl:BackColor = RGB(128, 0, 256).</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <p class=\"p\">For detailed information on programming ActiveX\nControls, see <cite class=\"cite\">OpenEdge Development: Programming Interfaces</cite> manual.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__notes_GC1A1682702816\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d492018e189\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">The\nRGB-VALUE function is generally most useful when it is used with ActiveX\nControls.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"RGB-VALUE-function__see-also_GC1A1692702820\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d492018e198\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"COLOR-TABLE-system-handle.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/COLOR-TABLE-system-handle.html\">COLOR-TABLE system handle</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"RETURN-VALUE-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/RETURN-VALUE-function.html\">RETURN-VALUE function</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"RIGHT-TRIM-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/RIGHT-TRIM-function.html\">RIGHT-TRIM function</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310534","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1318,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"RGB-VALUE function","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/RGB-VALUE-function.html","type":"Manual"}